      "writtenOn": "2023-11-09T17:32:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I picked this just because FDT spec says `phandle` is mostly auto-generated:\n\n```\nMost devicetrees in DTS (see Appendix A) will not contain explicit phandle properties. The DTC tool automatically inserts the phandle properties when the DTS is compiled into the binary DTB format.\n```\n\nWould you prefer to have explicit phandle? Then I can simplify code bit further because we can know phandles of `pviommu` without iteration.\n\nBTW, if we place manually generated phandles, what would be the range of their phandles? Is there any standard? Otherwise I can use arbitrary range such as `0xF0` ~ `0xF9`",
      "parentUuid": "171a4f0d_675c4a49",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 265,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 265,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "e649d976521dbc87849fe01877dfefbb856c1b10",
